+
+Baseline generator SHA-256 `691464f74c800a3f6ec2948c67918c4667ad27dc74d54a0592fd134014bb0a8c` had two independent review defects. Its task tests assumed task-local canonical/base data and compared whitespace-formatted canonical source byte-for-byte; the portable staged command stopped before useful execution. The tests now locate their own runtime through `reviewer_support.find_root` / `canonical_path`, search both supported base-record layouts, and compare the selected Racket source by normalized semantics and pinned rule hash. The staged suite passes 16/16.
+
+The default IID sampler also left lesson-level shortcuts alive. In a protected canonical-Racket census over 54 three-demo/four-query windows, four explicit rivals (`nearest_parent`, `frames_only`, `first_group_only`, `global_largest`) produced 18 ambiguous baseline windows. Version 2.1.0 adds a deterministic three-profile curriculum: every three consecutive unoverridden draws contain a depth-3+ chain, at least two independent nesting groups, and a contained solid descendant. The same bounded census reports 0/54 ambiguous repaired three-demo windows. A retained baseline witness has `first_group_only` fit all three easy-band demonstrations and fail query 2.
+
+Evidence: `checks/d7c15b2e56ec-peer-learnability/report.json`, plus the staged red/green task-test receipts under `checks/d7c15b2e56ec-*`. The Racket audit executed 324 unique inputs and retained exact source hashes. This is finite rival coverage only; two-demo lessons still show survivors and remain outside `EXAMPLES_NEEDED=3`. Independent completion review also caught and fixed a curriculum regression: a known axis passed as `None` was being mistaken for an explicit override, although the shared generator API defines `None` as unset. All seven axes now normalize `None` before curriculum and keyed-draw decisions; the regression test failed 7/7 cases before the fix and the staged suite passes 16/16 afterward. Final proposed generator SHA-256 `4ea8443087b34e9e27d488b74b105e0befae6b883a53bfb88fa840006d78d836`.
+
+The source is a peer proposal, not owner-approved or training-admitted.
